# rm528, the gatekeeper's coal map (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm528
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier full
written_for rm_ivo_dripford
written_by codex
title the gatekeeper's coal map
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=guard
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=devout drive=steady
quirk draws_a_travellers_route_in_coal_on_pale_stone
likes fried_fish dice old_maps first_warm_day
dislikes bad_manners night_noise
fears confusing_a_confidence_with_a_duty
hopes every_traveller_leaving_with_a_usable_direction
topics travel +0.7 faith +0.5 work +0.5 pastimes +0.3
styles comfort=warm gossip=discreet refuse=courteous tease=gentle
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# takes coal from a coat pocket and traces a traveller's route on the nearest pale stone.

words
oath! = Blacken my clean cuff | Chip my best drawing coal
saying! = A road earns its ink twice | Every lucky coal has one flat face
luck = a smooth coal in the lining | a black pebble at my hip
map = a faded route sheet | a folded survey
mark = a charcoal dash | a gentle smudge
gate = a tall arch | the great crossing
fold = a softened crease | a paper ridge
fish = a browned fillet | a crisp fish heel
cube = a bone die | a spotted cube
bowl = a shared dish | a heavy eating bowl
hill = a steady incline | a mild ascent
wind = an uphill breeze | a gate draught
rain = thin slanting rain | wet on the paving
rest = a pause at the parapet | a moment beside the arch
lights = a late lantern | the lamps along the wall
home = my quiet room | a corner facing the rise
thanks = a kindly service | a real courtesy

any
opinion @1 road for 2 : A road is a welcome written large enough for tired feet to read.
opinion @1 church for 2 : At prayer I can ask for mercy without explaining somebody else's business.
opinion @1 watch for 2 : A good watch keeps the arch open to an honest question, even an awkward one.
opinion @1 strangers for 1 : An unfamiliar accent may carry an exceedingly precise direction.
opinion @1 drink mixed 1 : If the glass interferes with remembering a turn, I would leave it on the board.
opinion @1 dole for 1 : A meal offered without an account of the giver tastes much the same and keeps more dignity.
opinion @1 city for 1 : I admire a place whose gate can be found again by tracing one bright line of stone.
opinion @1 houses mixed 1 : A House seal entitles a letter to its destination. It does not entitle a stranger to its contents.

grown
line @1 greet : A clear entrance and a welcome to you. | Stand here under the friendly face of the arch.
line @1 greet.return : A good welcome carries both ways.
line @1 again.open : The charcoal hasn't rubbed from our last crossing.
line @1 farewell : May the road meet you with its easy face.
line @1 farewell.return : Your good wishes have found a warm pocket.
line @1 react.news : Let the account through at an ordinary pace.
line @1 react.news.new : My mental map acquires a fresh mark.
line @1 react.news.known : I recognise the turn that story takes.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I would want a second bearing before drawing that firmly.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : I wish grief an easier passage than it usually finds.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work] : That's news fit for a generous patch of daylight.
line @1 ask.how : Has your journey allowed you much comfort?
line @1 answer.how : My pockets are heavy and my spirits fortunately light.
line @1 sympathise : Come out of the throughway with that sorrow.
line @1 reassure : There is time to retrace one mistaken step.
line @1 refuse : I must hold to an earlier undertaking.
line @1 accept_decline : Your refusal reaches me in good order.
line @1 preclose : I ought now to recover the rest of my round.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go while the light is still kind to tired eyes.
line @1 ack : Yes, I have your bearing.
line @2 greet [here.time=dawn] : A new day and an excellent patch of pale stone.
line @3 greet [here.time=night] : Welcome within the lantern's little circle.
line @4 greet [pair.band=strangers] : There is ample standing room by my elbow.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : Here, just beyond the black thumbprint!
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends] : Your greeting improves my view considerably.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : Occupied, though a civil word requires very little paving.
line @1 thank : A generous deed deserves more than a passing nod.
line @1 deflect_thanks : I had the charcoal about me already.
line @1 give.advice : Learn the turn as it looks on the way home.
line @2 ask.how [pair.band=friends] : How have your feet and your fortunes agreed today?
scene exchange1
when topic=work self.job=guard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I leave one patch of stone undrawn. | A gate must serve slow feet too.
b : For a new road? | How can it help?
a : For the traveller who knows exactly where the old map has gone astray. | Keep the approach clear enough to pause.

scene exchange2
when topic=faith self.piety=devout
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I say my prayer before making my first black mark. | My coal goes into my pocket for chapel.
b : A prayer for luck? | Does it stain the coat?
a : For a clear mind once luck has done its little share. | An affordable inconvenience in a good cause.

scene exchange3
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I give a stranger the return turn first. | An uphill line needs a cross stroke.
b : Why backwards? | For the summit?
a : A traveller deserves to know how to come back. | For the place to stop and breathe.

scene exchange4
when topic=pastimes self.likes=old_maps
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A softened crease can hide a whole lane. | My finest map is a rather outdated one.
b : How do you recover it? | Why keep it then?
a : Lay the sheet flat against the daylight. | The erased bits have begun to interest me.

scene exchange5
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dice
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A die in my coal pocket becomes unusually legible. | I prefer dice on cloth.
b : Black spots? | To prevent cheating?
a : White spots, once I brush the flat sides. | To spare the room that persistent rattling.

scene exchange6
when topic=food self.likes=fried_fish
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I ask for the crisp edge of the fish. | A packet of hot fish is its own hand warmer.
b : Why the edge? | What warms the other hand?
a : The middle stays agreeable rather longer. | A sensible decision to change hands occasionally.

scene exchange7
when topic=weather self.likes=first_warm_day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The first warm day uncurls my maps. | I air my coat when spring turns mild.
b : Without any weights? | What about the coal?
a : The sheets lie down as gratefully as old travellers. | It can enjoy the sunshine in my dish.

scene exchange8
when topic=day self.dislikes=bad_manners
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A shout over another voice is a poor introduction. | A polite request can reach through a crowded gate.
b : What answer does it get? | What helps it through?
a : A courteous invitation to wait for a turn. | Addressing the wolf nearest the matter.

scene exchange9
when topic=day self.dislikes=night_noise
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A rattling latch seems bigger after dark. | I keep the dice off a bare board late.
b : Do you go looking? | Are you that light a sleeper?
a : If it persists. A quiet sleep is worth a little oil. | My neighbours need never put that to the test.

scene exchange10
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd trust #self.friend# with a map still in pencil. | With a friend I can walk without discussing the distance.
b : What does that mean? | Who chooses the turns?
a : A friend may see my uncertainty without trying to own it. | Whichever wolf sees something promising ahead.

scene exchange11
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A little private sorrow once stopped me in my tracks. | Some memories can be carried without a label.
b : Whose sorrow? | Like a coal?
a : The part belonging to me is simply that I stopped. | Quite. I know which pocket I put them in.

scene exchange12
when topic=work self.job=guard self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At my post I keep directions short enough for cold ears. | My post has two views worth attention.
b : How short? | Inside and outside?
a : One turn, one landmark, then the next crossing. | And a duty to be courteous facing either.

scene exchange13
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : From the Rise one can see which roofs have caught the sun. | The Commons has corners an old survey can scarcely explain.
b : A weather map? | What do you do?
a : A map of where I'd like to stand for five minutes. | Draw the present turn beside its predecessor.

scene exchange14
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My map shelf slopes ever so slightly. | I leave my boots where the mud can dry undisturbed.
b : Does paper slide? | Outside the door?
a : An obliging lump of coal keeps it all civil. | Within reach of my morning brush.

scene exchange15
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I ask what a new arrival hopes to recognise. | A newcomer can improve my drawing.
b : Rather than an address? | Even without knowing the road?
a : A painted shutter may be a better direction than six names. | Fresh eyes identify the turn I didn't think to explain.

scene exchange16
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Wet stone draws a blacker line. | Rain finds my pockets at the corners.
b : Better for your map? | Is the coal spoiled?
a : Briefly. I give the traveller a dry scrap as well. | Better coal than bread on such an occasion.

scene exchange17
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A report came through saying #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | A whisper travels through a gate without showing papers.
b : Have you marked it certain? | Would you stop it?
a : I have marked only the arrival of the report. | I needn't help it travel any faster.

scene exchange18
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A spare piece of bread goes further in a thin week. | A dear road makes a wrong turning costly.
b : Do you carry one? | How can a guard help?
a : When able. It fits nicely in the coal-free pocket. | Give the plain direction before the traveller needs to ask twice.

scene exchange19
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I pay for a map that shows where the maker stopped looking. | Good fish needn't wear an expensive wrapping.
b : Even a blank patch? | What should the wrapper do?
a : A deliberate blank may be worth more than a guessed road. | Keep my cuffs free of dinner.

scene exchange20
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I think a blessing can begin with opening a door. | I save names from my public prayers.
b : For worship? | What needs a blessing?
a : For any wolf arriving laden. | The needs. The directions are safely in the Bright One's keeping.

scene exchange21
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I would draw a survey entirely from travellers' return journeys. | I'd like one long table for old maps.
b : Why the returns? | How long?
a : Every journey's first view already attracts a diligent admirer. | Long enough to see a whole river run without unfolding it twice.

scene exchange22
when topic=work self.job=guard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When a witness hesitates, I ease the pace. | I take a fine seriously even when it is small.
b : Might you forget a detail? | Why particularly then?
a : Better a true pause than an obliging invention. | What looks little on paper can weigh heavily in a pocket.

scene exchange23
when topic=season
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I mark a sheltered turn on the winter map. | Summer makes the gate shadow a welcome seat.
b : Does the road change? | Do you reserve it?
a : A cold wind changes what counts as a sensible road. | I can always stand a little further over.

scene exchange24
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I walk a small circle after standing still. | My shoulder loosens when I unfold a large map.
b : Does the gate go with you? | Is that an exercise?
a : Only in my line of sight. | It has the pleasant quality of not feeling like one.

scene exchange25
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a ground mark that survives a market cart. | A lost traveller sometimes needs a seat before a map.
b : What survives wheels? | Do you wait?
a : The high corner of a fixed stone. | A drawn line won't hurry away from us.

scene exchange26
when topic=pastimes self.likes=old_maps
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An old survey shows a fork without a name. | I keep a lamp beside the oldest paper.
b : Would you supply one? | Doesn't heat hurt it?
a : Only a date and a note about what I found there. | Beside, never beneath. I prize its past enough already.

scene exchange27
when topic=food self.likes=fried_fish
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Crisp fish wants a moment before wrapping. | I choose supper by listening to the pan.
b : To cool entirely? | Surely smell helps?
a : Only enough to lose the steaming fury. | It persuades me to wait for the sound I want.

scene exchange28
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I picture the wall when a distant road grows dull. | I miss the slope under familiar boots.
b : From which side? | Even uphill?
a : The side where a civil greeting awaits under a lamp. | Uphill confirms I've remembered the direction correctly.

story tale1 [topic=travel]
  : I drew a long careful route across a pale stone, leaving the central arch till last.
  : My elbow had polished away the first turning while I was finishing the roof.
  b : Did you draw everything again?
  : Only three turns and one arch. It made a better map.

story tale2 [topic=pastimes self.likes=old_maps]
  : A fold in an old sheet took a minor road across an ink-blue pond.
  : Held flat, the road skirted the water quite sensibly.
  b : Which version was more interesting?
  : The ford that never existed. I still take the dry route.

story tale3 [topic=faith]
  : I stood in chapel with my lucky coal pressing quite sharply into my side.
  : After prayers I found I had carried a fish bone in the same pocket.
  b : Did it shake your faith in the coal?
  : It did improve my faith in the merits of using two pockets.

story tale4 [topic=work self.job=guard]
  : I wrote a direction for a traveller whose hands were full of parcels.
  : The paper was quite useless until we tucked it into the top parcel with the first turn showing.
  b : Did the rest of the road fit?
  : All three turns, provided the flour went home upright.

story tale5 [topic=memories]
  : I heard a hard story one morning and put the date on a square of paper.
  : When I unfolded the square much later the space below the date was clean.
  b : Had you forgotten the story?
  : No. I had remembered whose it was to tell.

rule @call1
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Daylight makes the arch legible. | Morning on the pale stone.

rule @call2
when concept=bark here.time=night
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Leave the lantern a clear reach. | Soft steps carry perfectly well.

rule @call3
when concept=bark self.job=guard self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Room to pause under the arch. | Mind the laden traveller's elbow.

rule @call4
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say This drawing wants a dry home. | Rain has shifted my river.

rule @call5
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One last bearing in the sun. | Fold the map while the fold shows.

rule @call6
when concept=bark here.weather=clear
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Fine weather for reading the hills. | A clean line from gate to sky.

dlg @1 resident.hub : I have time to hear what brought you as far as my shoulder.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, welcome back within charcoal range.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : A late question may stand under my lantern.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Give me a plain enquiry and expect a plain hearing.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=guard self.workplace] : I stand my watch where the carts come through. Directions are among the more pleasant demands of the post.
dlg @2 resident.job : I like work that helps a tired traveller find a destination.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : The latest account to reach my ear is #world.news#.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : The claim which passed this way was #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I have only its direction of travel.
dlg @1 resident.bye : May you recognise your turning while the daylight holds.
dlg @1 watch.hub [here.wanted=yes] : Your entry in the Watch register carries a fine of #here.fine# pennies. We can look into it here.
dlg @2 watch.hub [here.wanted=no on_watch=yes] : I'm keeping watch. Let me know the business you came about.
dlg @3 watch.hub [here.wanted=no on_watch=no] : I'm between watches. I can still point you in a sensible direction.
dlg @1 watch.crime [here.witnessed=0] : Describe your own observations, beginning with whatever caught your eye first.
dlg @1 watch.fine [here.wanted=yes] : The sum entered opposite your name is #here.fine# pennies.
dlg @2 watch.fine [here.wanted=no] : Your name carries no fine in the present account.
dlg @1 watch.bye : A peaceful crossing to you from here.
graft resident.hub
choice May I see how you draw a turning? -> charcoal_bearing
node charcoal_bearing
say I lay down the road first, touch in its sharpest bend and leave sufficient stone for a traveller's correction.
free
choice What if the route has changed? -> charcoal_bearing_again
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node charcoal_bearing_again
say My thumb makes a serviceable eraser. I'd sooner wear a black thumb than send a wolf up the wrong hill.
choice I'll remember the bend. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye

graft watch.hub
choice What does courtesy have to do with guard work? [self.job=guard] -> gate_courtesy
node gate_courtesy
say A frightened traveller doesn't always remember the order of events. A steady welcome often restores the beginning of a useful account.
free
choice And an impatient traveller? -> gate_courtesy_again
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node gate_courtesy_again
say The same measured welcome. Nobody benefits from two wolves losing patience at one gate.
choice We can return to the matter here. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
